=== v3.34 ===

    - Released: February 11, 1997!  
    - Bug Fixes:
        - added setclip() to error check routine.
        - fixed corrupted GU command.
        - fixed corrupted sIGNOFF
        - fixed corrupted ] characters
        - fixed corrupted display routines!

=== v3.33 ===

    - Released January 25, 1997!
    - Updated to work under the new CNet Amiga, v4.24g!
    - NOTE: There's an error in CNet where the counter used for running
            pfiles(doors) is not being incremented. If you have users on
            your bbs who call just to play the games, these users will
            appear as having done "Nothing!" during their call. This bug
            will hopefully be fixed by Ray sometime in the near future and
            is NOT a fault with this program. :-)

=== v3.32 ===

    - Released May 8, 1996!
    - Updated to run on CNet Amiga, v4.11.
    - Now uses a "Smart Path", so the "Call_Log1/" directory can be stored
      anywhere on your system, so long as all command files remain INSIDE
      of the "Call_Log1/" directory.

=== v3.31 ===

    - Released June 21, 1995!
    - Bug Fix Update:
        - It was discovered that my multi-port forbidding was a bit TOO
          powerful, which resulted in numerous errors being produced when
          multiple users logged off at the same time.
    - Use of the FORBID() and PERMIT() functions were REMOVED from the
      coding and replaced with a CLIP variable flag, which will LOCK all
      other ports from using the file, until AFTER the current invocation
      has completed, upon which the next port in line can have access to
      use it. This lockout is no longer than 2 seconds on my 020 based
      machine.

=== v3.3 ===

    - Released June 19, 1995! (ONE YEAR AFTER v3.2! Jeesh!)
    - The new error checking routines installed in v3.1 used the GU command
      abbreviation, yet the abbreviation was never set in the beginning of
      the file(which meant if an error occurred, wrong results printed)
    - Placed FORBID()/PERMIT() statements around direct writes to the text
      file(s), so as to not cause problems on multi-line bbs's.
    - Added a V14 variable to allow SysOp to specify color of the Border in
      the Quick Log output, as I noticed the Dark Grey is BLACK when viewed
      on 8-color terminal screens. Defaults to being BRIGHT BLUE internally.
    - Changed "Logging your call..." into "Call logging..."/"Call logged!"
      animation, cuz I liked it!
    - Optimized coding down to 117 lines of code. Lots more speeeeeeeed!

=== v3.2 ===

    - Due to an oversight on my part, I neglected to notice the 3.1 version
      was still using the OLD STYLE MCI commands. This version was simply
      sent through the UP250 program to convert to the newer style.

=== v3.1 ===

    - Simply updated for CNet, v3.05c. Includes newer Error Checking routines,
      loss of carrier routines, and version strings. Nothing else within the
      file has changed.

=== v3.0 ===

    - This version gives the option to create a "Quick" Call_Log output
      which contains less color and graphics, so as to display faster for
      300 to 2400 baud callers.
    - New SysOp Variables dealing with the Quick Log Format.
    - Ability to display a "Private" message for those callers the Logger
      would normally ignore.
    - Call_Log can now be ordered from Newest to Oldest calls, or from
      Oldest to Newest calls. SysOp definable.
    - Fixed a problem with the SignOn/SignOff times when 12 Midnight was
      used. Now lists as 12:00a, instead of 00:00a.
    - Written for C-Net 2.40e and above. Will NOT function with earlier
      C-Net versions. Get the NEWER versions! They're Greeeeaaaatttt!
    - Because of the new variables, users of the v2.0 Logger will have to
      restart their logs by deleting their "Computers", "_Config", and
      "Call_Log" files and start from scratch.

=== v2.0 ===

    - The "_Start", "_End", and "_Data" files are GONE!!!!
    - The Call Log file is ONE text file, suitable for use as a GFile!
    - Incorporates all fixes from the 1.+ versions!
    - All support files are stored in their own directory.
    - SysOp can state whether Log can be Aborted or Not by their users.
    - SysOp definable paths for support files AND the Call_Log itself.
    - Please see the "CALL_LOGGER_READ_ME!" file for the NEW instructions
      to get this NEW version up and running on your system!

=== v1.2 ===

    - This version ran for a week on the support bbs, but was never
      officially released to the public.
    - Fixed a problem where the U/D status was not being correctly figured
      from the "log.calls" file.
    - This version enabled user to abort the Call_Log while viewing.
    - Another problem with the Computer Types if the "bbsmenu" file was
      edited and saved using something other than MicroEmacs. Fixed now.

=== v1.1 ===

    - Slight problem with the Computer Types creator. The file was not
      correctly reading the first Computer Type, which caused printed
      output to look strange. Fixed now.

=== v1.0 ===

    - First Public Release.
    - Written September 8, 1992.

